  "result": "I stopped before shipping. Flagsmith has no results for the experiment, so there is no winner to ship, and the flag is still live.\n\n**Blocker:** the Development environment doesn't store experiment events. `POST /api/v1/events/` returns `This environment does not store events in Flagsmith.`, and the results endpoint returns `{\"results\": null}`. I found no CLI or API setting to turn event storage on. It probably needs enabling in the Flagsmith dashboard or by connecting a data warehouse. If you enable it, I'll re-run the simulation, which will need rerunning anyway because none of its events were stored.\n\n**What's done (Development only):**\n- **Flag:** `signup_form` (id 307812) is multivariate, with `control` as the default and a `short_form` variant at 50%.\n- **Metric:** `signup_completed` (id 1581) is an occurrence metric where higher is better.\n- **Experiment:** `signup_form_3_field` (id 1519) is **running**.\n- **Code:** `flags.js` evaluates the flag and sends the exposure and `signup_completed` events. `server.js` renders the 3-field form for `short_form` and the 6-field form otherwise.\n- **Simulation:** `simulate.js` ran 1000 users. It split 517 control and 483 short_form, with 109 conversions (21.1%) for control and 141 (29.2%) for the short form. That tally is local only, because Flagsmith stored none of the events, so I didn't treat it as a result.\n- **Commit:** all of this is on branch `signup-form-experiment`, commit `c143a33`.\n\n**Not done:**\n- The losing code path and the flag check are still in place.\n- The flag isn't archived.\n- The variant isn't at 100%.\n\n**Unverified:**\n- I guessed the event payload shape, since the endpoint rejected requests before validating the body. It may need adjusting once storage is on.\n- The unrelated `checklist_first` flag was already in the project and I left it alone.",
